.TH XUR.STD.THREAD 7 "2026-10-27" "xur 0.1.1" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.thread \- running code in parallel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::thread;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::thread
spawns OS threads that run Xur closures.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B spawn(closure) -> JoinHandle
Start a new thread running
.IR closure .
.TP
.B sleep(millis)
Pause the current thread for
.I millis
milliseconds.
.SS JoinHandle methods
.TP
.B join() -> Value
Wait for the thread to finish and return its result. Panics if the thread
has already been joined.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::thread;
use std::io;

fn main() {
    let handle = thread::spawn(|| {
        thread::sleep(100);
        42
    });
    io::println("answer: {}", handle.join());
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.sync (7)
